# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "An image needs a source that holds something"

# image.js skips whitespace after the inner `[` and then reads `([^\]]+?)\]\]`, so a source holding
# nothing, or only whitespace, builds no image and TiddlyWiki keeps the brackets as text. A reader
# meets the brackets as the text they are.

A space: [img[ ]] here.
#        ^^^^^^^^ - markup.other.image.tiddlywiki5
#         ^^^ - keyword.other.img.tiddlywiki5

A space before the inner bracket too: [img [ ]] here.
#                                     ^^^^^^^^^ - markup.other.image.tiddlywiki5

Nothing at all: [img[]] here.
#               ^^^^^^^ - markup.other.image.tiddlywiki5

# CONTROL: a source carrying a title builds, whitespace around it and all.
An image: [img[ pic.png ]] here.
#         ^ punctuation.definition.image.outer.begin.tiddlywiki5
#          ^^^ keyword.other.img.tiddlywiki5

A tooltip with a blank source still builds: [img[tip| ]] here.
#                                           ^ punctuation.definition.image.outer.begin.tiddlywiki5
